 ```
 
-## Step 3: Promote the Replica
+| Reading | Action |
+| --- | --- |
+| `lag_seconds` under 5 | Continue to step 2. |
+| `lag_seconds` 5 to 30 | Wait 60 seconds and re-run. Continue when it drops under 5. |
+| `lag_seconds` over 30, primary reachable | Stop. Fix replication instead of failing over. |
+| `lag_seconds` over 30, primary down and lag not shrinking | Data loss on promotion equals the lag. Get an incident commander's approval in the incident channel before step 4. |
+| `lag_seconds` is null | The replica has replayed everything it received. Compare `received` and `replayed`; equal values mean it is caught up. Continue. |
 
-Now for the moment of truth. Promoting the replica is irreversible — once you do this, the old primary can no longer be reattached without a full rebuild.
+Record `replayed` in your scratch file. It is the recovery point.
 
