+## Step 3: fence the old primary
 
+Fencing stops the old primary from accepting writes. Skipping this risks two hosts accepting writes at once, which produces divergent data no tool reconciles.
+
+Reachable primary, stop Postgres:
+
 ```bash
-vim /etc/pgbouncer/pgbouncer.ini
-systemctl reload pgbouncer
+ssh db-primary.prod.internal 'sudo systemctl stop postgresql@16-main'
+ssh db-primary.prod.internal 'sudo systemctl is-active postgresql@16-main'   # expect: inactive
 ```
 
